; drops no table and adds no migration. Seven server surfaces moved, each named with where it lives
; (the seventh was added by review the same day, see PROMO_REPORT_NAME_DECIDED_AT):
;   1. the retired carousel's buttons already in chats answer with the rental menu and read no
;      table -- turbobaby/bot-surface, CAROUSEL_RETIRED_AT;
;   2. GET /api/loyalty/tiers serves every perks list empty (the stored perks are the old shop's
;      promises, and no TurboBaby perk copy is approved) and omits the tier named after the old shop
;      -- src/api/loyalty.rs, get_loyalty_tiers and retired_tier; the rows are untouched. This
;      closes the perks question DECISIONS.md left open on 2026-09-24;
;   3. the three public tech-tree reads answer an empty roadmap, an empty badge list and not found
;      -- src/api/tech_tree.rs; the rows are untouched and the admin complete route is unchanged;
;   4. the share card builds only from a catalogue row the public catalog shows (is_available), so
;      a row 085 hid answers not found -- src/api/share.rs, load_card;
;   5. the bot's admin heading loses the old catalogue's tab list and the fact-post reply its leaf
;      -- src/bot/commands.rs;
;   6. the bot locale file loses four fields: the carousel's heading and arrows, and the old unit
;      of sale -- src/locales.rs;
;   7. the owners' promo sales report -- the bot's /promo and GET /api/admin/promo-report -- no
;      longer prints the stored name of a published post about the product table migration 083
;      dropped -- src/trios/promo.rs report_kind_and_name, called by src/promo.rs report; the rows
;      stay and still count. The rule is PROMO_REPORT_NAME_* below.
; tests/server_text_vocabulary_wiring.rs holds every string the server can send to it from now on.
; Run through this file's machine, the tech tree is what bike sales were on 2026-09-24: rows kept,
; none hidden, masked on read, which is STATE_LIVE because no state names a mask on read (see
; A_MASK_ON_READ_HAS_A_STATE_HERE). The dropped strains table keeps its allowlisted reader --
; still compiled, with no production caller since item 1 -- which is STATE_READER_ALLOWLISTED, so
; ALLOWLIST_SIZE does not move. Nothing here is a completed retirement: COMPLETED_RETIREMENT_COUNT
; stays 1, and none of the route counts above moves, because every route stays declared.
