; --- Surface 7: the names the promo sales report prints ------------------------------------------
; DECIDED 2026-09-25 by the operator, applying the owner's ruling of that day; added by review the
; same day. The label printed in place of a withheld name is admin-facing copy chosen then, and is
; cited here by name (REPORT_WITHHELD_NAME in src/trios/promo.rs), not quoted.
;
; WHY. promo_posts keeps every row the promoter ever wrote, and from 2026-08-19 until migration 083
; it also wrote about the product table 083 dropped: rows of the kind whose subject variant left
; with 083, and bestseller rows drawn from that table. The report printed each row's stored
; subject_name -- the old shop's product name -- to the owners in /promo (30 days) and on the admin
; route (up to 365 days). Whether production holds such a published row today was not read; the
; rule does not depend on the answer.
;
; THE RULE, fail closed (report_may_print_name). A stored name is printed only when a subject the
; promoter can build today writes the row's kind AND the link stored with the row opens the
; deep-link kind a live post of that kind opens. A row with no stored link (drafted before
; migration 076) is judged by its kind alone, except a bestseller: bestsellers were drawn from two
; tables until 083 and only the link tells which. Otherwise the name is withheld; the kind is kept
; when a live subject writes it and printed empty when none does, because that word is the retired
; one or one nobody here classified (the database forked from another shop's bot, DECISIONS.md D19).
; No row is hidden, so the report's post count and totals do not move, and nothing in the table is
; written.
;
; WHAT IT DOES NOT DECIDE. Whether a stored draft may still be SENT: that is the Publish button's
; question, and the same day's item-13 decision in turbobaby/promo-broadcast answers it there
; (publish_refusal in src/promo.rs, refusing every stored kind). This file claims no line of
; publish. Names of posts about the old shop's other tables -- accessories, teas, sets, events,
; which migration 085 hid rather than dropped -- are still printed: this surface withholds only a
; name the dropped table supplied, and PROMO_REPORT_OTHER_TABLES_NAMES_PRINTED keeps that visible.
pub const PROMO_REPORT_NAME_DECIDED_AT : str = "2026-09-25";
pub const PROMO_REPORT_NAME_DECIDED_BY : str = "operator, applying the owner's ruling of 2026-09-25 (answer 12)";
pub const PROMO_REPORT_NAME_SITE : str = "src/promo.rs report";
pub const PROMO_REPORT_NAME_DECISION : str = "src/trios/promo.rs report_kind_and_name";
pub const PROMO_REPORT_NAME_LABEL : str = "src/trios/promo.rs REPORT_WITHHELD_NAME";
pub const PROMO_REPORT_NAME_WIRING_TEST : str = "tests/promo_report_names_wiring.rs";
pub const PROMO_REPORT_READER_COUNT : u8 = 2;
pub const PROMO_REPORT_ROWS_HIDDEN : bool = false;
pub const PROMO_REPORT_WRITES_THE_TABLE : bool = false;
pub const PROMO_REPORT_UNCLASSIFIED_KIND_IS_WITHHELD : bool = true;
pub const PROMO_REPORT_OTHER_TABLES_NAMES_PRINTED : bool = true;
pub const PROMO_PUBLISH_REFUSAL_OWNER_ID : str = "turbobaby/promo-broadcast";

pub fn report_prints_stored_name(kind_written_by_a_live_subject: bool, link_stored: bool, link_opens_the_kinds_table: bool, kind_spans_two_tables: bool) bool {
    if (!kind_written_by_a_live_subject) {
        return false;
    }
    if (link_stored) {
        return link_opens_the_kinds_table;
    }
    return !kind_spans_two_tables;
}

; --- The owner's answer of 2026-09-25 (#3): stored content out of customers' sight -------------
; Answer 3 of the second numbered list put to the owner on 2026-09-25 is quoted verbatim in the
; header of the rules' module (OWNER_ANSWER_3_RULES; this file stays ASCII). The operator read it
; as OWNER_ANSWER_3_READ_AS: analyse all the cannabis-era content a customer could still see from
; stored data, and take it out of sight without deleting or rewriting stored data. So every change
; stops SERVING or PRINTING something, in code; no row is written, deleted or hidden and no
; migration is added. The database was forked from the previous shop's bot (DECISIONS.md D19), so
; what it stores was not all written by this repository, and each rule fails closed: a customer
; is served what this code can vouch for. The admin views are the archive and read every row whole.
;
; THE ANALYSIS: every customer-facing read of stored legacy content in src/api and src/ui, and
; the bot sends that read it. Masked on the server, five (OWNER_ANSWER_3_SERVER_READS):
;   1. order lines of a retired kind on the customer's own list and detail
;      (GET /api/orders/user/:telegram_id and /api/orders/:id/details): the neutral name and the
;      stored quantity and unit price only. turbobaby/order-presentation owns the rule and its
;      name (RETIRED_LINE_*), which is why it is not restated here;
;   2. the shop those two reads name, withheld when it names the previous shop, as every value the
;      old checkout stored did -- the same section there;
;   3. the server cart (GET and POST /api/cart, POST /api/cart/merge): a line of a retired kind --
;      every kind the cart API accepts -- keeps its id and figures and is served the neutral name
;      and no picture. RECONCILED 2026-09-26, see below: such a line is not served at all, under
;      turbobaby/cart-persistence's rule, and nothing on a cart's path renames a line;
;   4. the bonus history (GET /api/loyalty/:telegram_id/bonus-history): a stored description is
;      served only when it is one of the four sentences this repository writes and serves, word for word
;      apart from its figures (OWNER_ANSWER_3_DESCRIBED_TX_TYPE_COUNT). A garden row's, the
;      welcome credit's (its sentence named the garden; since 2026-09-26 a new row stores a trimmed one
;      no owner worded, see below, and every welcome row is withheld on read), an admin-typed one and anything the previous shop's bot wrote are
;      withheld. The row's amount and date are served, and its type as read 5 says;
;   5. the same read serves a garden-era row's TYPE empty (customer_bonus_tx_type), so the row
;      reaches every bundle as a generic bonus: the profile's label function has labelled a type
;      it does not name with T_PROFILE_BONUS_OTHER since it first shipped on 2026-08-07, and the
;      garden's label is the one it would print for the stored type. This is what reaches a bundle
;      cached before answer 3, which withholding the description alone would not have reached;
;      the client guard below covers the bundles built after it.
; Guarded on the client, where it builds the text itself, four on this answer's branch; two since
; the reconciliation below removed the device-cart pair (OWNER_ANSWER_3_CLIENT_GUARDS):
;   the order screens print the neutral name in the reader's language; a garden-era bonus row
;   carries the generic label T_PROFILE_BONUS_OTHER instead of the garden's, whatever type a server
;   serves it, and the garden's key stays declared and translated and is printed by no screen; and
;   a cart kept on the device, written by an older bundle with the old item's name, prints the
;   neutral name on the cart and the checkout and draws no stored picture there either: both
;   screens read the line's picture through the server's own rule (cart_line_image), so the cart
;   row shows its placeholder and the checkout no image. A device cart outranks the server's masked
;   copy while it holds a line, and every kind the client's cart type knows is retired, so without
;   the fourth guard a stored picture -- an absolute storage address still resolves -- would sit
;   beside the neutral name. The one other reader of a device cart line, CartItemComponent, is
;   mounted by no screen; it reads the line through the same two rules, so mounting it cannot
;   bring the stored name or picture back.
; Analysed and left, six on this answer's branch, each with its reason; four since the
; reconciliation below, which names the two its neighbours closed (OWNER_ANSWER_3_LEFT_READS):
;   * the loyalty profile's stored tier key: the profile screen maps the old shop's key to a card
;     and prints the card's label, never the key; the leaderboard that serves it raw is read by
;     the admin screen alone -- and since 2026-09-26 answers an admin alone, enforced by R1
;     (turbobaby/loyalty-ledger, LEADERBOARD_GATE_SITES; OWNER_ANSWER_R1_* below);
;   * the star history (GET /api/stars/history/:telegram_id): no screen reads it, and none ever
;     did (no client file this repository has held calls it);
;   * the reads behind retired surfaces -- the bookings read, the quest locations, the legacy
;     catalog routes: no mounted screen renders them since 2026-09-24 and 2026-09-25, the catalog
;     reads answer only rows 085 left published, and whether those routes go is the question the
;     answer of 2026-09-25 (#7) left open (LEGACY_PATHS_REPOINTED_ON_2026_09_25 above);
;   * the abandoned-cart reminder, a bot send: it reminds a cart at most twice (its count never
;     resets), and since 085 hid the last kind the cart API accepts no cart line can be written, so
;     no reminder is left that could carry a stored name (CLOSED 2026-09-26 by
;     turbobaby/cart-persistence: the reason missed a cart kept from before 085);
;   * the referral, quest-scan and game reads: the referral and game reads are numbers, the
;     customers' own names and compiled-in text. The quest scan's reply does carry a stored name,
;     the scanned location's -- admin-typed and seeded by no migration -- but the kept quest prints
;     only whether the scan succeeded, beside checkpoint titles compiled into the bundle, never
;     that name;
;   * the referral notification worker's friend_watered arm, a bot send outside src/api and
;     src/ui: it prints the garden's sentence for a queued row of that kind. No code has written
;     the kind since D5 removed the garden, and the worker ends every row it hands out after three
;     passes, sent or not, so the arm can fire only for a row queued before D5 that was never
;     handed out. Not changed: no neutral sentence was given for it, and the one row it could
;     still reach is one nobody has shown to exist. CLOSED 2026-09-26 by
;     turbobaby/notification-queue, which holds such a row unsent.
; Nothing here retires a surface: every surface stays reachable and every row stays, so no state
; above moves (OWNER_ANSWER_3_CHANGES_A_STATE) and COMPLETED_RETIREMENT_COUNT stays as it is.
; RECONCILED 2026-09-26, when this answer's branch was merged with two changes of that day that
; reach further, so that the contracts say one thing:
;   * THE CART. The kept-cart change (turbobaby/cart-persistence, SERVED_CART_KINDS) serves no
;     line of a retired kind at all: the cart API neither lists nor sums one, the abandoned-cart
;     reminder neither sums nor names one, and the Mini App drops one from a saved cart and from a
;     server cart. Its rule was kept and this answer's cart path removed: the server cart's
;     neutral name and missing picture (read 3 above) and the two device-cart guards (the neutral
;     name and the stored picture on the cart, the checkout and CartItemComponent). A line that
;     never reaches a customer needs no name, and a served line is a rental line whose name and
;     picture are its own. The one place a line could still have entered the Mini App's cart
;     without that predicate, Cart::add_item (a reorder, or a screen nothing mounts), asks it too
;     since the same day, so no cart screen is handed such a line. OWNER_ANSWER_3_SERVER_READS
;     keeps read 3, which the neighbour now takes out of sight; the client guards are two.
;   * THE REMINDER. The fourth read left above said no reminder could carry a stored name, since
;     no cart line of a retired kind can be written. A cart kept from before 083 and 085 still
;     holds such lines, so the reminder could; the kept-cart change closed it (its reads join
;     only served lines, and a cart of hidden lines is never due).
;   * THE GARDEN'S NOTIFICATION ARM. The sixth read left above is closed by
;     turbobaby/notification-queue (HELD_KINDS_DECIDED_AT): a queued friend_watered row, and a row of
;     any kind nobody classified, is held unsent, and the garden's message left src/locales.rs.
; So four reads stay analysed and left, and the two the neighbours closed are named below.
pub const OWNER_ANSWER_3_AT : str = "2026-09-25";
pub const OWNER_ANSWER_3_READ_BY : str = "operator";
